This skill began as a fork of vox-explainer-skill by Kingsley
(https://github.com/CK42BB/vox-explainer-skill), MIT licensed.

What remains from that project is its premise: that a single topic prompt can drive a
complete narrated explainer film, staged as script -> voiceover -> artwork -> animation
-> assembly, with voiceover generated first because its length is the clock.

Everything in this repository has since been rewritten or newly written:

  * The artwork stage was inverted. Upstream generated a finished composition per beat
    and animated it; this generates ELEMENTS on a keyable field and composes locally,
    which is what makes real depth possible.
  * The multiplane renderer, scene graph, chroma keyer, sprite-sheet prompting, local
    paper-element factory, kinetic overlays and the reusable sprite library are new.
  * The provider stack is different (Higgsfield and local neural TTS rather than Atlas
    Cloud), and the format is vertical short-form rather than 16:9.
  * All prose in SKILL.md and the reference documents is newly written.

Upstream's own reference documents are not included here.
